FuncDef:
The network command imports routes to the BGP routing table and advertises them to peers.
The undo network command cancels the configuration.
By default, BGP does not import routes.
ParaDef:
{'Parameters': 'ipv6-address', 'Info': 'Specifies the IPv6 address of a route to be imported by BGP.\nThe prefix is in the format of X:X:X:X:X:X:X:X.'}
{'Parameters': 'prefix-length', 'Info': 'Specifies the mask length of an IPv6 address. If no mask length is specified, the IP address is considered as a classful address.\nThe value is an integer that ranges from 0 to 128.'}
{'Parameters': 'route-policy route-policy-name', 'Info': 'Specifies the name of a route-policy that is used for route import.\nThe name is a string of 1 to 200 case-sensitive characters, with spaces not supported. When double quotation marks are used around the string, spaces are allowed in the string.'}
{'Parameters': 'route-filter route-filter-name', 'Info': 'Specifies the name of the route-filter that is used for route import.\nThe value is a string of 1 to 200 case-sensitive characters, spaces not supported. If parameters are included in the referenced route-filter, specify values for them in the format of (var1, var2, ...var8) behind the route-filter name. A maximum of eight parameters can be specified, and each value ranges from 1 to 200 characters.'}
