## User question:
Configure Huawei router to advertise a default IPv6 route to BGP peer 2001:DB8:2::2 only when either of two conditional routes (2001:DB8:A::/48 or 2001:DB8:B::/64) is matched in the routing table.
---
## Proposed answer:
ipv6 route-static 2001:DB8:A:: 48 Null0
ipv6 route-static 2001:DB8:B:: 64 Null0
route-policy CONDITIONAL_DEFAULT permit node 10
if-match ipv6 address prefix-list ROUTE_A_OR_B
apply ipv6 next-hop 2001:DB8:2::2
quit
ip ipv6-prefix ROUTE_A_OR_B index 10 permit 2001:DB8:A:: 48
ip ipv6-prefix ROUTE_A_OR_B index 20 permit 2001:DB8:B:: 64
bgp
peer 2001:DB8:2::2 route-policy CONDITIONAL_DEFAULT export
commit
