## Router configuration manual:
CLIs:
peer <ipv6-address> tracking [ delay <delay-time> ]
undo peer <ipv6-address> tracking
FuncDef:
The peer tracking command enables BGP Peer Tracking. That is, you can configure BGP to fast detect the unreachable state of a peer and re-establish the connection between the local device and the peer.
The undo peer tracking command disables BGP Peer Tracking.
By default, BGP Peer Tracking is disabled.
ParaDef:
{'Parameters': 'ipv6-address', 'Info': 'Specifies the IPv6 address of a peer.\nThe value is a 32-digit hexadecimal number, in the format of X:X:X:X:X:X:X:X.'}
{'Parameters': 'delay delay-time', 'Info': 'Indicates the interval between when BGP detects the peer unreachable and when BGP tears down the corresponding connection.\nThe value is an integer that ranges from 0 to 65535, in seconds. The default value is 0 seconds.'}
---
