CLIs:
peer <ipv6-address> capability-advertise add-path { both | receive | send }
undo peer <ipv6-address> capability-advertise add-path { both | receive | send }
FuncDef:
The peer capability-advertise command enables optional BGP functions when a BGP peer advertises routes to its peer. The optional BGP functions include route-refresh, general router function, 4-byte AS number, and Add-Path.
The undo peer capability-advertise command restores the default setting.
By default, the route-refresh and 4-byte AS number functions are enabled, but the general router function and Add-Path are disabled.
ParaDef:
{'Parameters': 'ipv6-address', 'Info': 'Specifies the IPv6 address of a peer.\nThe value is a 32-digit hexadecimal number, in the format of X:X:X:X:X:X:X:X.'}
{'Parameters': 'add-path', 'Info': 'Indicates the Add-Path function.\nadd-path takes effect only on IBGP peers.\n-'}
{'Parameters': 'both', 'Info': 'Enables the RR to receive Add-Path routes from and send Add-Path routes to a specified IBGP peer.\n-'}
{'Parameters': 'receive', 'Info': 'Enables the RR to receive Add-Path routes from a specified IBGP peer.\n-'}
{'Parameters': 'send', 'Info': 'Enables the RR to send Add-Path routes to a specified IBGP peer.\n-'}
